    "cancrops:handbook-guide-title": "CANCrops: Genetics and Breeding",
    "cancrops:handbook-guide-text": "CANCrops adds a genome to every crop. Seeds carry stats, a species pair and resistance, all of which you can improve through selective breeding.\n\n<strong>Genome</strong>\nFive numeric stats — <font color=\"#aaffaa\">Gain</font>, <font color=\"#aaffaa\">Growth</font>, <font color=\"#aaffaa\">Strength</font>, <font color=\"#aaffaa\">Resistance</font>, <font color=\"#aaffaa\">Fertility</font> — plus a Species pair. Every gene has a dominant and a recessive allele; only the dominant value affects the plant, but the recessive one is passed on.\n\n<strong>Seed tooltip</strong>\nHover a seed to see its stats, species (with carried recessive in brackets), the effective light range (MinLight–MaxLight ±tolerance × Strength), and the cold/heat damage thresholds adjusted by Resistance.\n\n<strong>Cross-breeding</strong>\nPlace Selection Sticks next to grown crops. Each tick the sticks check neighbouring mature plants and may spawn a mutated seed on themselves, based on configured cross-breeding rules (parent pair + chance + conditions). Place the result in farmland to grow the new species.\n\n<strong>Clipping</strong>\nUse shears on a mature crop to collect extra seeds without uprooting the plant. The clipped seed inherits the parent genome with small per-stat variance — useful for stabilising a sorted lineage.\n\n<strong>Cultivator</strong>\nThe hand cultivator removes weeds from infested crops or selection sticks.\n\n<strong>Mushrooms</strong>\nThirteen mushroom species can be discovered by crossing pairs of vanilla crops or basic mushrooms. They will only grow if <font color=\"#ffcc66\">bonysoil</font> is placed directly under the farmland block. They tolerate any light level within their range (MaxLight 9–14) — most accept full darkness."
